course: dictionary
lesson: 5894
title: Māori: a people, a language, a describing word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Māori is one word that can do three jobs. It can name a people: the Māori are the Indigenous people of New Zealand (Aotearoa), who were living there long before Europeans arrived. It can name a language: te reo Māori is the language of the Māori people.
explain: It can also describe things. In «Māori songs» or «Māori art», the word Māori is an adjective, and it tells you the songs or art belong to this people and culture. Look at the words around it to see which job it is doing: a name, a language, or a describing word.
explain: «The hongi is a traditional Maori greeting in New Zealand, done when you are invited.» Here the clues tell you what a hongi is. It is a greeting, it is traditional, and it happens in New Zealand. You do not need to know it already to understand the sentence.
fact: «Māori» names the Indigenous people of New Zealand (Aotearoa), who lived there long before Europeans arrived.
fact: «Māori» is also the name of the language, te reo Māori.
fact: As an adjective, «Māori» describes things that belong to this people and culture, like «Māori songs» and «Māori art».
fact: «Kia ora» is a Māori greeting that means hello, and «whānau» means family.
fact: The hongi is a traditional Māori greeting where people press noses and foreheads together.
exercise: «Kia ora» is a Maori greeting used in New Zealand. What does kia ora mean? | Goodbye and see you soon | Thank you very much | Sorry I am late | *Hello and good health
exercise: In New Zealand schools, children learn te reo Māori words such as whānau. What does whānau mean? | Canoe | Food | Song | *Family
exercise: Find the describing word in «Māori songs and art». Which word is it? | songs | art | and | *Māori
test: «The hongi is a traditional Maori greeting in New Zealand, done when you are invited.» What is a hongi? | A type of food | A dance performed by a rugby team | A kind of canoe | *A greeting where people press noses and foreheads together
test: «Māori (te reo Māori) is also their language.» What is te reo Māori? | A Māori greeting | A Māori song | *The Māori language | The name of a New Zealand city
exam: «Māori are the Indigenous people of New Zealand, who were living there long before Europeans arrived.» What does Indigenous mean here? | They came to New Zealand from Europe | *They were the first people living there | They only visit New Zealand | They are the newest people in New Zealand
